# A world with a pending scheduled tick is not quiescent, and running to
# quiescence must advance far enough to fire it.
#
# Quiescence is how the product will decide a door has finished moving, so
# "stopped early" and "never stops" are both product bugs, not just engine bugs.

bounds 0 0 0 7 7 7

schedule 2 2 2 delay=4 priority=normal
expect not_quiescent

run_until_quiescent 100

expect quiescent
expect stop quiescent

# 5, not 4. The tick scheduled for tick 4 fires *during* tick 4, and tick_count
# reports completed ticks — so once tick 4 has finished, the counter reads 5.
# Written out because this off-by-one is precisely the kind that would make every
# reported door timing one tick wrong.
expect tick 5
